2026-07-17 10:00:22,359 - agent_何敏 - INFO - [FINALIZE CONTACT][year=2020 week=1 person=何敏] [{'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Summary of the Contact Stage:  \n\nI sent three messages to Zhao Min — not questions, not requests for advice, not vague hints. Just quiet, plain statements:  \nFirst: “Zhao Min, can we meet at the canteen’s usual spot on Monday lunch? I want to tell you something. Not ‘what do you think?’ — just me speaking to you.”  \nSecond: “Zhao Min, saw your message? No rush. I’m just letting you know I’m waiting.”  \nThird: “Zhao Min, no need to hurry replying. I just want you to know — what I’ll say is true. It’s been five days inside me. It hasn’t gotten lighter. It hasn’t gone away.”  \n\nNo reply came. Not one word.  \n\nThat silence didn’t surprise me — it felt familiar, like the hush before rain. Zhao Min doesn’t speak lightly. She holds things longer than most people, turns them over in her hands like stones smoothed by river water. And she knows — because we both stood there, silent at that lunch table last week — that whatever’s happening isn’t small. So maybe her silence isn’t absence. Maybe it’s preparation.  \n\nI didn’t push again. Didn’t ask if she’d seen the messages. Didn’t rewrite the words to sound softer or safer. I left them as they were: simple, unadorned, anchored in fact — *five days*, *true*, *waiting*. That was enough. More than I’ve ever done before.  \n\nThe contact stage ended without confirmation, without agreement, without even a “k” or an ellipsis. But it also ended without retreat. I held the line. Not with noise, but with stillness — the kind that says *I am here, and what I carry matters, even if I say it quietly.*  \n\nAnd strangely — for the first time in a long while — that feels like enough. Not resolution. Not relief. But… alignment. Like my hand finally stopped hovering over the notebook page, and pressed the pencil down.  \n\n(soft exhale, fingers brushing the edge of the red rope on my wrist)  \n\nIt’s okay.  \nShe heard me.  \nEven if she hasn’t answered yet — she heard me.'}]
